  "articleBody": "You’ve heard all about structured data and schema, and maybe you've even tried implementing some on your site. But if you're still not seeing your business cited by AI overviews or answer engines, something might be off. Structured data is supposed to give AI explicit clues about your content, but a lot of businesses make common mistakes that actually hinder their visibility. It's like speaking a language but using the wrong grammar – AI just can't understand you properly.\n\nOne big pitfall is using structured data that doesn't actually match the visible content on your page. AI systems are smart; they'll notice if your schema claims you offer a service that isn't clearly explained on the page itself. Another common error is adding irrelevant or unsupported schema properties, trying to game the system rather than accurately describing your business. And, of course, inconsistent business names, addresses, or phone numbers (your NAP info) across your website and external profiles can really confuse AI about who you are and where you operate. AI builds a picture of your business as an \"entity,\" and if that picture is fuzzy, it's less likely to recommend you confidently.\n\nCommon Mistakes to Avoid\nTo truly optimize your website entity for AI, avoid these common mistakes. First, never use structured data that contradicts the actual content people see on your page – honesty is key for AI trust. Second, don't just sprinkle schema haphazardly; every piece of markup should accurately describe something specific about your business, service, or location. Third, be meticulously consistent with your business name, address, and phone number (NAP) across all online platforms, including your website, social media, and directories. Inconsistent information creates ambiguity for AI. Finally, remember that simply adding schema isn't enough; it needs to be validated and kept up-to-date, especially after any website changes or rebranding. If you're struggling to get it right, that's when a professional can really step in to ensure your structured data is a clear, unambiguous beacon for AI systems.\n\nCurious if your structured data is working for you? Let's take a look together.",
  "datePublished": "2026-09-23"
